From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Leave through exit() when a process ends itself on PS5.

NtTerminateProcess on the current process, without ExitProcess's first
call for the other threads, ends in abort_process, which is _exit(). The
title restarts into its launcher from its exit handlers, which _exit
skips, so an unhandled exception (kernelbase's filter, once it cannot
start winedbg, terminates the process this way) took the whole title
down with the game: Battle.net's crash after sign-in left the console at
its home screen instead of the launcher.

The other threads are now ended first, as ExitProcess does, and the
process leaves through exit_process, so the exit handlers run.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
index a11cc77666..2ff204ba24 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
@@ -989,7 +989,19 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtTerminateProcess( HANDLE handle, LONG exit_code )
     {
         if (!handle) process_exiting = TRUE;
         else if (process_exiting) exit_process( exit_code );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+        else
+        {
+            /* _exit skips the exit handlers a title restarts into its
+             * launcher from, so an unhandled exception took the whole title
+             * down. End the other threads first, as ExitProcess does, then
+             * leave through exit(). */
+            NtTerminateProcess( 0, exit_code );
+            exit_process( exit_code );
+        }
+#else
         else abort_process( exit_code );
+#endif
     }
     return ret;
 }
